"THE NATURAL JOIN HAS A NAME (2026-09-07). theta:NatJoin built its join as an anonymous form -- flatten over ALPHA over (join_combine, a Filter on the key, distl) over distr, the nested loop over both row lists -- and handed it to apply, so no host could recognise the join to answer it any faster: the boot's rule closure over the support store ran 20 million COMP applications inside derive:form_join in twenty seconds, all of them that loop. theta:NatJoin now builds the form (theta:natjoin keys), and theta:natjoin, reached through tau clause (c) with the form and the argument, applies the old builder's form exactly as before; a host with a twin for theta:natjoin answers the same rows by hashing the right list on its first column, in the same order. theta:natjoin0 is the builder as it was.",

