"The ABSORB TARGETS of a partition: the distinct tables something OTHER than themselves maps into, sorted. A fact type that maps to itself is its own table and absorbs nothing, so the f == t pairs drop -- keeping them would name every own-table as an absorber, which is the whole distinction rmap:colfts/rmap:coltables rest on. Sorted because the host held these in a HashSet and then sorted, so the order was never the set's; lambda sorting makes the answer deterministic without the host owing the sort.",
