"The ENTITY/OWN split, engine/rust's classification (main.rs): own = the declared fact types that no table absorbed, sorted; entity tables = every declared entity PLUS every absorbing table that is not itself an own-table fact type. Cell-level, so NOT rmap:absorbed or rmap:otindep -- those derive from rmap:assim and rmap:otmeta at model level, while these read what a compile already materialized. Order is irrelevant for the entity tables (the host holds them in a set) but load-bearing for own, which is why only that one sorts.",
