"WHICH FACT TYPE ANSWERS AUTHORIZATION -- A DESIGNATION, NOT A SCHEMA. Lambda must not hardcode apps/access's own fact type names: RBAC is one rule shape and ownership, tenancy and time-boxed grants are the same hook with a different rule, all of them derived populations reached by the same lfp, none of them a policy engine. So lambda names the CELL where an app says which fact type answers <caller, operation, resource>, and the app populates it. This is the metamodel's own binding idiom -- `Derivation Rule is provided by Constraint` at core.md:949 binds one thing to another as an instance fact -- applied to authorization. THE READING IS THE APP'S (2026-09-09): the cell was named AuthorizationIsAnsweredByFactType after a reading no file declared, so no app could ever designate; `App answers authorization with Fact Type` (readings/templates/organizations.md, beside App's other facts) is the binding an app asserts -- `App 'support' answers authorization with Fact Type 'User is authorized'` -- and the app's auth context, in Sam's words, is exactly that fact.",
