"AND THE PATH IS SEARCHED, NOT DECLARED. The matcher above takes <keyPos, keyValue, valPos> as given; something has to supply them. Samuel, on whether a matching rule should be declared instead: the two are the same except with tolerance, with the single-matcher being a 100% -- so the search IS the strict case of one mechanism, not a rival design, and a declaration would only relax it later. What is searched: every fact type carrying a role played by the WANTED type, and within it every other position, for the known value. A position holding the value proposes whatever sits at the wanted position. Nothing needs emitting for this -- state:declared already says which type plays which role, and a value that is not there simply proposes nothing.",
