"AND A COLLECTION READS AS ITS ROWS (2026-09-11). A GET of a word in ui:groups answered rows: [] -- support's Plan, Error Code, every table with a population -- because this read system:pop_rows, and a table is not a fact type: it has no population of its own. So POST took an entity whole and GET could not give one back, which is the same half-door the entity tool was written to close. The rows of a table are its WIDE rows, rmap:group_for's fifth slot, one per key value with a slot per member of rmap:members_of -- Sam's db row that is a lot like a high arity complex fact -- and building them for ONE key is 0 to 3 ms on support against the 53% of a first screen that building every group once cost. A NAME THAT IS BOTH now reads as the table, because main:api already POSTs it as one and a resource that writes one way and reads another is worse than either: PlanProduct answers <Starter/vin, 0.004>, its row, where it answered <Starter, vin>, and the objectification's two role players are exactly what its key spells.",
"A COLLECTION`S ROW ANSWERS EVERY VALUE OF A MULTI-VALUED COLUMN, AND A READ OF ONE KEY READS ONE ROW (2026-10-02; the retention report: GET of a Cancel Request answers one value per multi-valued column). A GET of a table read its wide rows through rmap:wide_row, whose slot for a relation is the first of its member pairs on the key, which is the relational map`s row and right for a column, which has one value. A table`s members include relations that hold several values per key, Cancel Request has PostHog Session Recording and the request-log counts among them, so a Cancel Request with six recordings answered one, and one of its thirty request-log rows. The read`s row is main:wide_all, every member pair on the key, so a column answers its one value as before and a relation all of its own. And a read whose filler names a key builds that key`s row alone (main:table_keys), where it built every row of the table and then kept one: with every value read, all 786 Cancel Request rows take 0.11 to 0.15 s warm on support`s retention copy, and one row 0.002 s. Operand of main:table_rows and main:table_keys: <store, table, fillers>; of main:wide_all: <key, relations>; of main:slot_all: <relation, key>.",
