"THE VERDICTS RIDE ON THE RESOURCE THEY JUDGE. AREST.tex:260 lists the components of repr(e): the selectors on its facts, the derived facts, the constraint violations, and links(e). GET answered rows and links and no violations, so a store carrying 832 violations at rest answered every read as if it were whole; and the outcomes domain's Violation fact types answered 0 rows because nothing records a violation there, nor should a closure: a recorded Violation occurred at exactly one Timestamp, which a pure function of the store cannot mint, so those fact types are the RECORD of an evaluation, while the verdict at rest is a function of the store and is read, not stored. A read now carries the verdicts at the fact type it reads -- uniqueness and mandatory from that fact type's own descriptor, deontic and subset from the rules whose first leg is that fact type -- and so costs the fact type, not the store: ui:violations over a 959-fact-type store is 5.8 s, 4.5 s of it the mandatory arm, and no read may pay it. Operand <store, factType>; the rows are the same <factType, kind, subject> the commit gate answers.",
